def tsp(dist):  # dist[i][j] = cost from city i to city j
    n = len(dist)
    dp = [[float('inf')] * n for _ in range(1 << n)]
    dp[1][0] = 0  # start at city 0, only city 0 visited
    for mask in range(1 << n):
        for last in range(n):
            if dp[mask][last] == float('inf'):
                continue
            for nxt in range(n):
                if mask & (1 << nxt):
                    continue  # already visited
                new_mask = mask | (1 << nxt)
                new_cost = dp[mask][last] + dist[last][nxt]
                dp[new_mask][nxt] = min(dp[new_mask][nxt], new_cost)
    return min(dp[(1 << n) - 1][last] + dist[last][0] for last in range(n))
```

This is O(n² * 2ⁿ) — a huge improvement over the O(n!) of trying every permutation directly, and the standard baseline for exact TSP on small n.
